{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_76aaf847bf733c892162aade675cab31d8c0e6edc7873c64ec95b14ee3c8d206"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ./notify tool writes a structured JSON payload to a queue, and a post-run scripts/notify-deliver.sh is the only place channel tokens are consumed, rendering per channel (Telegram, Discord, Slack, Buzz) with per-send audit lines."},{"claim_ids":["clm_94152b4b1bee22d28bb277eaf4cc2b6954eeecca1001e294cf3ad36d73464262"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Aeon dispatches to ten coding-agent CLIs via a run-harness contract, including Cursor, Hermes, GLM, and Vercel's fx, with credentials surfaced as dashboard Access Keys rows."}],"claim_ids":["clm_76aaf847bf733c892162aade675cab31d8c0e6edc7873c64ec95b14ee3c8d206","clm_94152b4b1bee22d28bb277eaf4cc2b6954eeecca1001e294cf3ad36d73464262"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_a7ff5177c808486eb94ae3877caa7aae","id":"pg_32d66fcfaeac501682d6131bbf52e1be","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/aeonfun-aeon-changelog-md-95142d19705c-131bbf52e1be.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c9a609665f5a5c32be294059aa11ef70"],"title":"aeonfun/aeon/CHANGELOG.md @ 95142d19705c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a7ff5177c808486eb94ae3877caa7aae"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_090d7ba6aace523cc012b625ea653f96f6fdefb3e480064748b7f260ba8a6bf4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"workflow_dispatch returns 204 with no run id, so integrators must either poll the runs list by dispatch time or subscribe to the workflow_run webhook for exact correlation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_237bb214a120db62f18f37f0ce3d8441c4cc38d3d4e8f5ee302771f8ef008b9f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ADK auth pattern uses three credentials: a user OAuth token (no scope param, since permissions come from the App definition), an App JWT used only to mint installation tokens, and a ~1h installation token scoped to one installation's repos."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2ed9ba23f17ddc20849fc9047515cdcffbdec3b18bc9ce8f93ff7a408afade1b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On-demand skill runs go through a single aeon.yml workflow accepting workflow_dispatch inputs: skill (required, regex-checked), var, model (must match a choice option or GitHub returns 422), and harness (claude default or grok)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4b0dd74d164e45d121a5fc9927ef055d5f5eb5c77446f71deab2b378e39722fc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"catalog/skills.json is the machine-readable skill catalog; each entry carries a slug, description, category, a single universal var input, required env keys, and needed MCP servers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8317142fd9228a982dcdfe7b990c2471db09c8c05f0be94eb28f83076f04b871"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ADK recommends a GitHub App over personal access tokens: no credential custody, least-privilege fixed permissions, instant revocation on uninstall, and free multi-tenancy since GitHub tracks installations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_84bbdb21091952122b79b586d18a485f7c850aaeda3a11a5605ebbb28fef2d89"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: pack authors can pre-flight locally with scripts/validate-pack.sh from an Aeon checkout, and listing requires a PR adding a README Community Packs row plus a catalog/skill-packs.json entry."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8524fb1b262679e3fac671019cd367fd0d69680faf901154f15bf6ce77e7f856"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A skill is a single Markdown file with frontmatter (name, description, category, requires, var, mode) plus a prompt; there is no plugin API or compilation step."},{"claim_ids":["clm_873544ab4ac9bced1a9d81bc9e86088baf051f80e0ec65b1cd1d6f5f59c9bfd2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tenant isolation requires re-verifying with the user's token on every request that they still have access to the stored installation/repo, because otherwise any authenticated user could drive someone else's agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a8da15adaa4c4cf4254aec05b68ff86678c6f4557b33f58641dd211e3af2c14"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The instance needs at least one model credential (CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, or an LLM gateway key), resolved by prefix with auto-cascading."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dca220d4e9a1e4aa481d33e90b5d416ee54dcf72048b5889e9c26f6ff669613a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An Aeon instance is a GitHub repo plus GitHub Actions with no Aeon server or API; integrators read/write files and dispatch workflows via GitHub APIs such as Contents, Actions Secrets, and workflow_dispatch."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ebab8a19ea9bb1f24897b6cc00b85303329a790a21b4e4e24c1d0ee80829faf3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"GitHub delivers only about 10% of 5-minute schedule ticks; the scheduler also accepts repository_dispatch type cron-tick so a backend can act as an uptime pinger, with a debt model preventing double-firing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f5eea402cf66e85fe3a35855ce71c966c67f9fdaa4800195c1a8b7b05e6607d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skill packs are published in their own repo with a skills-pack.json manifest; the installer security-scans each SKILL.md, records provenance in skills.lock, and registers skills disabled so the operator remains the trust boundary."}],"claim_ids":["clm_090d7ba6aace523cc012b625ea653f96f6fdefb3e480064748b7f260ba8a6bf4","clm_237bb214a120db62f18f37f0ce3d8441c4cc38d3d4e8f5ee302771f8ef008b9f","clm_2ed9ba23f17ddc20849fc9047515cdcffbdec3b18bc9ce8f93ff7a408afade1b","clm_4b0dd74d164e45d121a5fc9927ef055d5f5eb5c77446f71deab2b378e39722fc","clm_8317142fd9228a982dcdfe7b990c2471db09c8c05f0be94eb28f83076f04b871","clm_84bbdb21091952122b79b586d18a485f7c850aaeda3a11a5605ebbb28fef2d89","clm_8524fb1b262679e3fac671019cd367fd0d69680faf901154f15bf6ce77e7f856","clm_873544ab4ac9bced1a9d81bc9e86088baf051f80e0ec65b1cd1d6f5f59c9bfd2","clm_9a8da15adaa4c4cf4254aec05b68ff86678c6f4557b33f58641dd211e3af2c14","clm_dca220d4e9a1e4aa481d33e90b5d416ee54dcf72048b5889e9c26f6ff669613a","clm_ebab8a19ea9bb1f24897b6cc00b85303329a790a21b4e4e24c1d0ee80829faf3","clm_f5eea402cf66e85fe3a35855ce71c966c67f9fdaa4800195c1a8b7b05e6607d5"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_a7ff5177c808486eb94ae3877caa7aae","id":"pg_499c1f89e3785e5e9cbceed8619d1463","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/aeonfun-aeon-docs-adk-md-95142d19705c-eed8619d1463.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_19bc9bacb4c45f59996178d8d573d3cf"],"title":"aeonfun/aeon/docs/ADK.md @ 95142d19705c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a7ff5177c808486eb94ae3877caa7aae"}
